    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1009">

                <pb facs="1025" n="905" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg905"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Jay to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-02-23"><hi rendition="#italic">February 23,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 997.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your instruction, No. 761, of the 7th instant, on the subject of the recent
                    interference with Bible colportage in Turkey.</p>
                <p>I have the pleasure to report that, since the writing of my dispatch of January 5
                    in this connection, there have been no further cases of interference with
                    colporteurs reported up to date to this legation or to the British embassy.</p>
                <pb facs="1026" n="906" xml:id="pg906"/>
                <p>I succeeded in January in securing the immediate and unconditional surrender of
                    the Bibles seized at various points in the Empire.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Peter Augustus
                    Jay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
